# Render a Velocity template

The `dependency:render-dependencies` goal renders a [Velocity](https://velocity.apache.org/engine/2.4/user-guide.html)
template with the resolved dependencies of the project. The template sees the dependencies, sorted by group ID,
artifact ID and version, as `$artifacts`, and a
[CollectionTool](https://velocity.apache.org/tools/3.1/apidocs/org/apache/velocity/tools/generic/CollectionTool.html)
as `$sorter`. The following execution writes a YAML list of the jars:

```xml
<project>
  [...]
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-dependency-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <id>render-libs</id>
            <phase>process-resources</phase>
            <goals>
              <goal>render-dependencies</goal>
            </goals>
            <configuration>
              <template><![CDATA[
#[[deps:
  jars:
#foreach($dep in $sorter.sort($artifacts, ["artifactId:asc"]))
#set($type = $dep.type)
#if(!$type || $type.trim().isEmpty())
  #set($type = "jar")
#end
#set($classifierSuffix = "")
#if($dep.classifier && !$dep.classifier.trim().isEmpty())
  #set($classifierSuffix = "-$dep.classifier")
#end
  - local:///opt/test/libs/$dep.artifactId-$dep.baseVersion$classifierSuffix.$type
#end]]#]]></template>
            </configuration>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
  [...]
</project>
```

After `mvn process-resources`, the build log shows the rendered template:

```text
[INFO] deps:
  jars:
  - local:///opt/test/libs/commons-lang3-3.14.0.jar
  - local:///opt/test/libs/commons-text-1.12.0.jar

[INFO] Wrote file '/path/to/project/target/template'.
```

The `template` parameter takes the template inline, as above, or the path of a template file. Without `outputFile`,
the result is printed to the log. The `classifier` parameter, `template` by default, also attaches the result to the
project with the `extension` parameter as its type, `txt` by default, so that it is installed and deployed with the
main artifact; set `classifier` to an empty value to skip that.

The goal selects the dependencies the same way as [dependency:build-classpath](../build-classpath-mojo.html), with
the same filter parameters.
